{"id": "EUVD-2026-92060", "enisaUuid": "07f4a199-ae87-37b4-a10d-3b0436d9f458", "description": "ezBookkeeping 1.2.0 before 2.0.1 contains a privilege escalation vulnerability that allows attackers holding an API token to obtain a full session token via /api/v1/tokens/refresh.json. Because TokenRefreshHandler never checks token type, attackers can exchange short-lived or IP-restricted API tokens for 30-day normal session tokens that bypass API token expiry and allowlists.", "datePublished": "2026-10-04T01:20:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-05T20:29:26", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/mayswind/ezbookkeeping/security/advisories/GHSA-wq25-mpcf-2mfc", "https://github.com/mayswind/ezbookkeeping/commit/9a92b07be8a7034665abfdb35b036210a1d57bf9", "https://github.com/mayswind/ezbookkeeping/releases/tag/v2.0.1", "https://github.com/mayswind/ezbookkeeping/blob/v2.0.0/pkg/api/tokens.go#L327-L380", "https://github.com/mayswind/ezbookkeeping", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/mayswind-ezbookkeeping-1.2.0-before-2.0.1-privilege-escalation-via-token-refresh-endpoint"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-105131", "GHSA-983g-gj75-pg7f"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2fc14699-5999-3cb1-95f2-f89904920605", "product": {"name": "ezBookkeeping", "vendor": {"name": "mayswind"}}, "product_version": "1.2.0 <2.0.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c1ef48a9-2dca-3c1a-9845-8be9996341e2", "vendor": {"name": "mayswind"}}], "isExploited": false}